@* View transitions (o.ViewTransitions = true wraps each navigation's re-render in
   document.startViewTransition). Each tile carries a unique view-transition-name and the detail
   hero re-declares the SAME name, so the browser morphs one into the other - the whole
   shared-element wiring is that pair of CSS names, with no animation code. *@

<h1>View transitions</h1>

<div class="gallery">
    @foreach (var item in GalleryCatalog.Items)
    {
        <BrouterLink Href="@($"/gallery/{item.Id}")" class="tile"
                     style="@($"background: {item.Gradient}; view-transition-name: item-{item.Id};")">
            @item.Emoji
        </BrouterLink>
    }
</div>

<p class="muted">
    Click a tile: it morphs into the detail hero while everything else cross-fades. Browsers
    without the View Transitions API navigate identically, just without the animation.
</p>
